{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 468 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "f0df61dec451d2c923b3b999be3ff702736b9650e16ca0805c76a46106a5c2fb" :edb/db-before-t 467 :edb/db-after-t 468 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533780 50 #inst "2026-10-04T22:48:49.595Z" 13194139533780 true] [17592186092187 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250626 13194139533780 true] [17592186092331 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250638 13194139533780 true] [17592186092332 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250633 13194139533780 true] [17592186092454 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533780 true] [17592186092454 1145 "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2}+x)=4x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(1)=4(1)+1=5,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-3 & =-\\frac{1}{5}(x-1) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{5}x+\\frac{1}{5}+3 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{5}x+\\frac{16}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5}x+\\frac{16}{5} & =0 \\\\ x & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the $x$-axis at $(16,0).$" 13194139533780 true] [17592186092671 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533780 true] [17592186092671 1145 "Let $f(x)=2{x}^{5}-2x.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{5}-2x)=10{x}^{4}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(1)=10(1)^{4}-2=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{′}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{8}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-0 & =-\\frac{1}{8}(x-1) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{x}{8}+\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a+b=-\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{1}{8}=0.$" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250626 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250627 13194139533780 true] [17592186250626 1089 "q-103546" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250626 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533780 true] [17592186250626 1100 "The equation of the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}$ at the point $(1,4)$ is given by $x+py=q$ where $p$ and $q$ are constants. Find the value of $q-p.$" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250626 1113 #uuid "b47ace4f-daa7-598e-bbed-f1675b554697" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250626 1145 "Let $f(x)=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(1,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(1)=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{1}^{3}}}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{′}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-4 & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-1) \\\\ 2y-8 & =x-1 \\\\ x-2y & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $q-p=-7-(-2)=-5.$" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250627 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250628 13194139533780 true] [17592186250627 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250629 13194139533780 true] [17592186250627 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250630 13194139533780 true] [17592186250627 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250631 13194139533780 true] [17592186250627 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250632 13194139533780 true] [17592186250627 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533780 true] [17592186250627 1041 "selection" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250627 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250628 13194139533780 true] [17592186250627 1110 #uuid "0f5a2264-cb7f-53b9-9781-3b162d6a86ac" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250628 1034 "-5" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250628 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533780 true] [17592186250628 1111 #uuid "578b5719-0cac-5261-a927-7d4e10f39141" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250629 1034 "3" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250629 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533780 true] [17592186250629 1111 #uuid "4a27c8ce-7896-529a-94ce-b4ecc3a15302" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250630 1034 "8" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250630 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533780 true] [17592186250630 1111 #uuid "b52e8744-54f9-5ff3-86c1-455fcd4db1d7" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250631 1034 "-4" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250631 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533780 true] [17592186250631 1111 #uuid "dd66e824-ede1-5352-a635-86372541d76d" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250632 1034 "-1" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250632 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533780 true] [17592186250632 1111 #uuid "ef119395-e0b3-5ba8-93f6-995c3da1f6cc" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250633 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250634 13194139533780 true] [17592186250633 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250636 13194139533780 true] [17592186250633 1089 "q-308823" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250633 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533780 true] [17592186250633 1100 "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{2}{x}+1$ at the point $(1,3)$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe normal line intersects the $x$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250633 1113 #uuid "f216eb4b-9d53-5b6d-b67a-8fb8e17cde01" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250633 1145 "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2}{x}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{-1}+1) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{-2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(1)=-\\frac{2}{(1)^{2}}=-2,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-3 & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-1) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{2}+3 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{5}{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the  $x$-axis at $(\\,-5,0\\,).$" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250634 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250635 13194139533780 true] [17592186250634 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533780 true] [17592186250634 1041 "field-1" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250634 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250635 13194139533780 true] [17592186250634 1110 #uuid "dc778d3b-c76e-5b55-9f39-91e81a4665e5" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250635 1034 "-5" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250635 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533780 true] [17592186250635 1111 #uuid "c62c4e05-1829-5405-9851-68156c959f02" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250637 13194139533780 true] [17592186250636 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533780 true] [17592186250636 1041 "field-2" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250636 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250637 13194139533780 true] [17592186250636 1110 #uuid "4534d582-f3a2-5fbf-9714-ac9aa89ce12a" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250637 1034 "0" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250637 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533780 true] [17592186250637 1111 #uuid "1c768d91-fad4-581e-85b7-08bc025ad0db" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250638 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250639 13194139533780 true] [17592186250638 1089 "q-342153" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250638 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533780 true] [17592186250638 1100 "Find the slope ${m}^{′}$ of the normal line to the curve $y=4-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}$ at the point $(\\frac{1}{4},2).$\n\n${m}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250638 1113 #uuid "ef7987ad-e618-5dff-80f2-97375df03f78" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250638 1145 "Let $f(x)=4-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4-{x}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(\\frac{1}{4},2):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(\\frac{1}{4})=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3}}}=4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope ${m}^{′}$ of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{′} & =-\\frac{1}{m} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250639 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250640 13194139533780 true] [17592186250639 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533780 true] [17592186250639 1041 "field-1" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250639 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250640 13194139533780 true] [17592186250639 1110 #uuid "d748d196-19c3-5676-b153-1d4c82fecd7f" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250640 1034 "-\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139533780 true] [17592186250640 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533780 true] [17592186250640 1111 #uuid "755785d3-b212-5cf0-92cd-6a1e0b14657a" 13194139533780 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-103546" 17592186250626 "q-103546/selection" 17592186250627 "q-103546/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" 17592186250628 "q-103546/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" 17592186250629 "q-103546/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" 17592186250630 "q-103546/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" 17592186250631 "q-103546/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" 17592186250632 "q-308823" 17592186250633 "q-308823/field-1" 17592186250634 "q-308823/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" 17592186250635 "q-308823/field-2" 17592186250636 "q-308823/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc4